le  and i think that will at its center be  about listening to young people in the  way that we have on this program tonight  and actually listening to their worries  so that we're responding  to you know where they are um in their  return to school in this process if we  connect  which we're all as teachers and support  staff really looking forward to  um no teacher enjoys teaching over a  laptop okay  i'm sorry to interact we're just about  to run out of time ellie sorry a final  quick thought from you on that as well  absolutely i mean school is about so  much more than education  it's about mental health physical  activity for some kids it's about  food and avoiding some of the aspects of  poverty  and i think this pandemic should have  really brought that home  to all of us as adults and it absolutely  has to be a priority  coming out of the pandemic okay thank  you so much sorry to rush you all there  but i'm afraid that is  all we have time for on this edition of  covid and the classroom so  all that's left for me to do is thank  our panel this evening  david laws rachel warwick and ellie  cannon thank you very much and also  thank you  to all of our contributors who sent in  their questions from home  and to you for watching us do remember  though we have full coverage of bryce  johnson's announcement on  the way ahead that's right here on sky  news on monday

